Data Source Type Use it when Query written to the dataset Report Data Provider The rows need X++: calculations, aggregation, business logic, data from several sources combined into a temporary table. <code>SELECT * FROM &lt;Class&gt;.&lt;TempTable&gt;</code> or <code>SELECT &lt;fields&gt; FROM &lt;Class&gt;.&lt;TempTable&gt;</code> Query The rows are a selection or join of tables with no X++ calculation; users filter through the query dialog. <code>SELECT * FROM &lt;Query&gt;</code> or <code>SELECT &lt;fields&gt; FROM &lt;Query&gt;</code> Enum Provider A parameter that shows the values of an enum. The enum name, for example <code>NoYes</code> <p>The metadata enum also has Business Logic and Database Stored Procedure. F&amp;O Studio doesn't pick a source for those; it tells you to type the Query in the property.</p> <p>A minimal data provider for a dataset looks like this:</p> <pre><code>[SRSReportParameterAttribute(classStr(ContosoCustGroupContract))]
class ContosoCustGroupDP extends SrsReportDataProviderPreProcessTempDB
{
    ContosoCustGroupTmp custGroupTmp;

    [SRSReportDataSetAttribute(tableStr(ContosoCustGroupTmp))]
    public ContosoCustGroupTmp getCustGroupTmp()
    {
        select custGroupTmp;
        return custGroupTmp;
    }

    public void processReport()
    {
        // Fill custGroupTmp here.
    }
}
</code></pre>
